Language-based security. Heavy on semantics, logics, types, and sometimes concurrency.

## Concepts

- Information-flow control & non-interference
- Capability-based security (E, Joe-E)
- Secure multi-party computation languages
- Zero-knowledge proof languages (Circom, Noir)

## Dependency

Types + Program logics + Concurrency -> Language-based security

## Resources

- Sabelfeld & Myers survey papers; language-based security books/notes - information-flow control
- E & Joe-E docs; capability papers via SIGPLAN - capability-based security
- MPC language papers (e.g. from PETS/CCS/POPL); language docs for specific MPC DSLs
- Circom/Noir docs; ZK-PL papers from security & PL venues (via ACM DL) - ZK proof languages
